# The shims are written to the customer's machine byte-for-byte and run by
# /bin/sh (Git Bash on Windows), which fails on CRLF. Check everything out LF
# everywhere: Windows runners default to autocrlf, which turned every
# text file into CRLF at checkout and made the installed shim -- written LF
# on purpose -- differ from its own source.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.bin binary
*.pem binary
